{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>From there they journeyed to Hagidgad.</b> It is not Hor Hagidgad, rather it is a general name [for] Tzalmona, also Punon and Ovot." "And <b>Yotvatah</b> is the place called Be'er, for so it is written: \"and from there to Be'erah,\" and this is the meaning of <b>a land of streams of water,\" for with their staves the nobles dug and the waters came out. And this verse, \"and from there they journeyed to Hagidgad,\" is joined with \"and Elazar ministered,\" and behold I have explained to you that Israel did not offer sacrifices after their journeying from Mount Sinai, and it is possible that they offered them when they came to Tzalmona and Punon, and the beginning of Elazar's service in the high priesthood was in those places on Rosh HaShanah, and he served in the place called Be'er on Yom HaKippurim. And behold, the interpretation is thus: \"and Elazar ministered\" when they journeyed to such-and-such a place — and why did Elazar minister? Because HaShem set apart the tribe of Levi at the time of the sin of the calf, to carry the Ark, to stand before HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:00.236256538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}